  ('pci-dss','3.4.1','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','PAN is masked when displayed','PAN is masked when displayed (the BIN and last four digits are the maximum number of digits to be displayed), such that only personnel with a legitimate business need can see more than the BIN and last four digits.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','3.4.2','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Copy and relocation of PAN via remote access is prevented','When using remote-access technologies, technical controls prevent copy and/or relocation of PAN for all personnel, except for those with documented, explicit authorization and a legitimate, defined business need.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.5.1','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','PAN is rendered unreadable wherever stored','PAN is rendered unreadable anywhere it is stored by using one-way hashes, truncation, index tokens, or strong cryptography with associated key management.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','3.5.1.1','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Keyed cryptographic hashes of PAN','Hashes used to render PAN unreadable (if used) are keyed cryptographic hashes of the entire PAN, with associated key-management processes and procedures in accordance with Requirements 3.6 and 3.7.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.5.1.2','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Disk-level encryption of PAN is limited','If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used to render PAN unreadable, it is implemented only on removable electronic media, or where used on non-removable media, PAN is also rendered unreadable via another mechanism that meets Requirement 3.5.1.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.5.1.3','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Disk encryption on removable media','If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used to render PAN unreadable on removable electronic media, logical access is managed separately and independently of native operating system authentication and access control, and keys are not stored on the media.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.6.1','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Cryptographic keys protecting stored account data are secured','Procedures are defined and implemented to protect cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data against disclosure and misuse.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','3.6.1.1','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Cryptographic architecture is documented','Additional requirement for service providers only: a documented description of the cryptographic architecture is maintained, including details of algorithms, protocols, keys, and key strength.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.6.1.2','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Secret and private keys are stored securely','Secret and private keys used to protect stored account data are stored in one or more forms: encrypted with a key-encrypting key at least as strong, within a secure cryptographic device, or as key components under split knowledge and dual control.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','3.6.1.3','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Access to cleartext key components is restricted','Access to cleartext cryptographic key components is restricted to the fewest number of custodians necessary.','technical','high'),
