  ('pci-dss','3.7.4','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Key changes at end of cryptoperiod','Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include cryptographic key changes for keys that have reached the end of their cryptoperiod.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.7.5','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Key retirement, replacement, or destruction','Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include the retirement, replacement, or destruction of keys when their integrity has been weakened or they are suspected of being compromised.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.7.6','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Manual cleartext key operations use split knowledge and dual control','Where manual cleartext cryptographic key-management operations are performed, these operations are managed using split knowledge and dual control.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.7.7','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Unauthorized key substitution is prevented','Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include the prevention of unauthorized substitution of cryptographic keys.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','3.7.8','Requirement 3: Protect Stored Account Data','Key custodians acknowledge responsibilities','Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include that cryptographic key custodians formally acknowledge (in writing or electronically) that they understand and accept their key-custodian responsibilities.','governance','low'),

