  ('pci-dss','7.1.1','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Security policies and procedures for Requirement 7 are documented','All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 7 are documented, kept up to date, in use, and known to all affected parties.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','7.1.2','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Roles and responsibilities for Requirement 7 are assigned','Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 7 are documented, assigned, and understood.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.1','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Access control model is defined','An access control model is defined and includes granting access based on the entity''s business and access needs, based on job classification and function, and assigning the least privileges required.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.2','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Access is assigned by job classification and least privilege','Access is assigned to users, including privileged users, based on job classification and function, and the least privileges necessary to perform job responsibilities.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.3','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Required privileges are approved','Required privileges are approved by authorized personnel.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.4','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','User accounts and access are reviewed','All user accounts and related access privileges, including third-party/vendor accounts, are reviewed at least once every six months to confirm they remain appropriate and inappropriate access is addressed.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.5','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Application and system accounts are managed','All application and system accounts and related access privileges are assigned and managed based on the least privileges necessary for the operability of the system or application.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.5.1','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Application and system account access is reviewed','All access by application and system accounts and related access privileges is reviewed periodically (at a frequency defined in the entity''s targeted risk analysis) to confirm access remains appropriate.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','7.2.6','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Query access to stored cardholder data is restricted','All user access to query repositories of stored cardholder data is restricted through application or programmatic methods and only to responsible administrators explicitly authorized to directly access or query repositories.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.3.1','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Access control system is in place','An access control system(s) is in place that restricts access based on a user''s need to know and covers all system components.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.3.2','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Access control system enforces assigned permissions','The access control system(s) is configured to enforce permissions assigned to individuals, applications, and systems based on job classification and function.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','7.3.3','Requirement 7: Restrict Access to System Components and Cardholder Data by Business Need to Know','Access control system defaults to deny all','The access control system(s) is set to "deny all" by default.','preventive','high'),

  -- Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access
  ('pci-dss','8.1.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Security policies and procedures for Requirement 8 are documented','All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 8 are documented, kept up to date, in use, and known to all affected parties.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.1.2','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Roles and responsibilities for Requirement 8 are assigned','Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 8 are documented, assigned, and understood.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Unique IDs are assigned','All users are assigned a unique ID before access to system components or cardholder data is allowed.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.2','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Shared and generic accounts are managed','Group, shared, or generic accounts, or other shared authentication credentials, are only used when necessary on an exception basis and are managed (need justified, use by individuals confirmed, and accountability maintained).','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.3','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Service providers use unique authentication per customer','Additional requirement for service providers only: service providers with remote access to customer premises use unique authentication factors for each customer premises.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.4','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','User ID lifecycle changes are managed','Addition, deletion, and modification of user IDs, authentication factors, and other identifier objects are managed with appropriate authorization and implemented only as authorized.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.5','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Access for terminated users is revoked','Access for terminated users is immediately revoked.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.6','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled','Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled within 90 days of inactivity.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.7','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Third-party remote access accounts are managed','Accounts used by third parties to access, support, or maintain system components via remote access are managed: enabled only during the time period needed, monitored while in use, and disabled when not in use.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.2.8','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Idle sessions require re-authentication','If a user session has been idle for more than 15 minutes, the user is required to re-authenticate to re-activate the terminal or session.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Access is authenticated with at least one factor','All user access to system components for users and administrators is authenticated via at least one authentication factor: something you know, something you have, or something you are.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.2','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Authentication factors are rendered unreadable','Strong cryptography is used to render all authentication factors unreadable during transmission and storage on all system components.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.3','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','User identity is verified before factor changes','User identity is verified before modifying any authentication factor.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.4','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Invalid authentication attempts are limited','Invalid authentication attempts are limited by locking out the user ID after not more than 10 attempts, and the lockout duration is set to a minimum of 30 minutes or until the identity is confirmed.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.5','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Passwords are set and reset securely','If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors, they are set and reset for each user securely: a unique value is set for first-time use and upon reset, and must be changed immediately after first use.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.6','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Password complexity minimums','If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors, they meet a minimum length of 12 characters (or eight if the system cannot support 12) and contain both numeric and alphabetic characters.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.7','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Password history is enforced','Individuals are not allowed to submit a new password/passphrase that is the same as any of the last four passwords/passphrases used.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.8','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Authentication policies are communicated','Authentication policies and procedures are documented and communicated to all users, including guidance on selecting strong factors, protecting them, and not reusing them.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.9','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Single-factor passwords are periodically changed','If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for user access, then either they are changed at least once every 90 days, or the security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed and real-time access decisions are made accordingly.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.10','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Guidance for customer single-factor passwords','Additional requirement for service providers only: if passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access to cardholder data, guidance is provided to customers on changing passwords periodically and when there is suspicion of compromise.','governance','low'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.10.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Customer single-factor passwords are changed or dynamically analyzed','Additional requirement for service providers only: if passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access, then either passwords are changed at least once every 90 days, or the security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed to determine real-time access.','preventive','low'),
  ('pci-dss','8.3.11','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Authentication tokens are managed','Where authentication factors such as physical or logical security tokens, smart cards, or certificates are used, they are assigned to an individual user and not shared, and physical/logical controls ensure only the intended user can use them.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','8.4.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','MFA for non-console administrative access to the CDE','MFA is implemented for all non-console access into the CDE for personnel with administrative access.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.4.2','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','MFA for all access into the CDE','MFA is implemented for all access into the CDE.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.4.3','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','MFA for remote network access','MFA is implemented for all remote network access originating from outside the entity''s network that could access or impact the CDE.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.5.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','MFA systems are configured to prevent misuse','MFA systems are implemented such that they are not susceptible to replay attacks, cannot be bypassed by any users unless documented and authorized for a limited time, use at least two different types of factors, and require success of all factors before access is granted.','technical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.6.1','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Interactive login by system/application accounts is managed','If accounts used by systems or applications can be used for interactive login, they are managed: interactive use is prevented unless needed for an exceptional circumstance, is limited to the time needed, business justification is documented, and use is explicitly approved and confirmed.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.6.2','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Credentials are not hard-coded','Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts that can be used for interactive login are not hard-coded in scripts, configuration/property files, or bespoke and custom source code.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','8.6.3','Requirement 8: Identify Users and Authenticate Access to System Components','Application and system account credentials are protected','Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts are protected against misuse by being changed periodically (per targeted risk analysis) and upon suspicion or confirmation of compromise, and are constructed with sufficient complexity appropriate for how frequently they are changed.','preventive','medium'),

  -- Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access
  ('pci-dss','9.1.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Security policies and procedures for Requirement 9 are documented','All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 9 are documented, kept up to date, in use, and known to all affected parties.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.1.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Roles and responsibilities for Requirement 9 are assigned','Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 9 are documented, assigned, and understood.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.2.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Facility entry controls are in place','Appropriate facility entry controls are in place to restrict physical access to systems in the CDE.','physical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','9.2.1.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Physical access to sensitive areas is monitored','Individual physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE is monitored with either video cameras or physical access control mechanisms (or both), and the collected data is reviewed and correlated with other entries and retained for at least three months.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.2.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Publicly accessible network jacks are restricted','Physical and/or logical controls are implemented to restrict use of publicly accessible network jacks within the facility.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.2.3','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Physical access to networking hardware is restricted','Physical access to wireless access points, gateways, networking/communications hardware, and telecommunication lines within the facility is restricted.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.2.4','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted','Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted via locking when not in use.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.3.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Physical access for personnel is authorized and managed','Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing physical access of personnel to the CDE, including identifying personnel, managing changes to access requirements, and revoking access.','physical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','9.3.1.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Access to sensitive areas is controlled','Physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE for personnel is controlled: access is authorized based on job function, revoked immediately upon termination, and all physical access mechanisms are returned or disabled.','physical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','9.3.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Visitor access is authorized and managed','Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing visitor access to the CDE, including that visitors are authorized before entering, escorted at all times, and clearly identified and given a badge that expires.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.3.3','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Visitor identification is surrendered on exit','Visitor badges or identification are surrendered or deactivated before visitors leave the facility or at the date of expiration.','physical','low'),
  ('pci-dss','9.3.4','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Visitor logs are maintained','Visitor logs are used to maintain a physical record of visitor activity within the facility and within sensitive areas, including the visitor''s name, the organization represented, and the personnel authorizing access, and are retained for at least three months.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Media with cardholder data is physically secured','All media with cardholder data is physically secured.','physical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.1.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Offline media backups are stored securely','Offline media backups with cardholder data are stored in a secure location.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.1.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Security of offline media backups is reviewed','The security of the location where offline media backups with cardholder data are stored is reviewed at least once every 12 months.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Media is classified by sensitivity','All media with cardholder data is classified in accordance with the sensitivity of the data.','administrative','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.3','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Media sent outside the facility is secured','Media with cardholder data sent outside the facility is secured: sent by secured courier or other delivery method that can be accurately tracked, with management approval prior to moving the media.','physical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.4','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Movement of media is approved by management','Management approves all media with cardholder data that is moved outside the facility (including when media is distributed to individuals).','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.5','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Inventory of electronic media is maintained','Inventory logs of all electronic media with cardholder data are maintained.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.5.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Media inventories are conducted','Inventories of electronic media with cardholder data are conducted at least once every 12 months.','detective','low'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.6','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Hard-copy materials are destroyed','Hard-copy materials with cardholder data are destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons, by cross-cut shredding, incineration, or pulping so that the data cannot be reconstructed.','corrective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.4.7','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Electronic media is destroyed','Electronic media with cardholder data is destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons via secure wiping, degaussing, or physical destruction so that data cannot be reconstructed.','corrective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.5.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','POI devices are protected from tampering','POI devices that capture payment card data via direct physical interaction with the payment card form factor are protected from tampering and unauthorized substitution.','physical','high'),
  ('pci-dss','9.5.1.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','List of POI devices is maintained','An up-to-date list of POI devices is maintained, including make and model, location, and serial number or other method of unique identification.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.5.1.2','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','POI device surfaces are inspected','POI device surfaces are periodically inspected to detect tampering and unauthorized substitution.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','9.5.1.2.1','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','Frequency of POI inspections is risk-based','The frequency of periodic POI device inspections and the type of inspections performed is defined in the entity''s targeted risk analysis.','detective','low'),
  ('pci-dss','9.5.1.3','Requirement 9: Restrict Physical Access to Cardholder Data','POI personnel are trained on tampering','Training is provided for personnel in POI environments to be aware of attempted tampering or replacement of POI devices, including verifying the identity of third-party repair personnel and reporting suspicious behavior.','administrative','medium'),

  -- Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access
  ('pci-dss','10.1.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Security policies and procedures for Requirement 10 are documented','All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 10 are documented, kept up to date, in use, and known to all affected parties.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.1.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Roles and responsibilities for Requirement 10 are assigned','Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 10 are documented, assigned, and understood.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Audit logs are enabled and active','Audit logs are enabled and active for all system components and cardholder data.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture access to cardholder data','Audit logs capture all individual user access to cardholder data.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture administrative actions','Audit logs capture all actions taken by any individual with administrative access, including any interactive use of application or system accounts.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.3','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture access to audit logs','Audit logs capture all access to audit logs.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.4','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture invalid access attempts','Audit logs capture all invalid logical access attempts.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.5','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture credential changes','Audit logs capture all changes to identification and authentication credentials, including creation of new accounts, elevation of privileges, and changes/additions/deletions to accounts with administrative access.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.6','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture audit log initialization and state changes','Audit logs capture all initialization of new audit logs, and all starting, stopping, or pausing of the existing audit logs.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.1.7','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Logs capture system-level object changes','Audit logs capture all creation and deletion of system-level objects.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.2.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Audit logs record required detail','Audit logs record the following for each auditable event: user identification, type of event, date and time, success and failure indication, origination of event, and the identity or name of affected data, system component, resource, or service.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.3.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Read access to audit logs is limited','Read access to audit log files is limited to those with a job-related need.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.3.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Audit logs are protected from modification','Audit log files are protected to prevent modifications by individuals.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.3.3','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Audit logs are backed up to a central server','Audit log files, including those for external-facing technologies, are promptly backed up to a secure, central, internal log server(s) or other media that is difficult to modify.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.3.4','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','File integrity monitoring on audit logs','File integrity monitoring or change-detection mechanisms are used on audit logs to ensure existing log data cannot be changed without generating alerts.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.4.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Security-relevant logs are reviewed daily','Security events, logs of all CDE system components, logs of critical systems, and logs of servers/system components performing security functions are reviewed at least once daily.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.4.1.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Log reviews are automated','Automated mechanisms are used to perform audit log reviews.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.4.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Other system component logs are reviewed periodically','Logs of all other system components (those not specified in Requirement 10.4.1) are reviewed periodically.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.4.2.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Frequency of periodic log reviews is risk-based','The frequency of periodic log reviews for all other system components (not defined in 10.4.1) is defined in the entity''s targeted risk analysis.','detective','low'),
  ('pci-dss','10.4.3','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Exceptions and anomalies are addressed','Exceptions and anomalies identified during the review process are addressed.','corrective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.5.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Audit log history is retained','Audit log history is retained and available for analysis for at least 12 months, with at least the most recent three months immediately available for analysis.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.6.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','System clocks are synchronized','System clocks and time are synchronized using time-synchronization technology.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.6.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Systems are set to consistent correct time','Systems are configured to the correct and consistent time: one or more designated time servers are in use, only designated central servers receive time from external sources, and time is distributed internally from those servers.','technical','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.6.3','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Time synchronization settings are protected','Time synchronization settings and data are protected: access to time data is restricted, and changes to time settings on critical systems are logged, monitored, and reviewed.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','10.7.1','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Service providers detect and respond to security control failures','Additional requirement for service providers only: failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.7.2','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Failures of critical security controls are detected','Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly, including network security controls, IDS/IPS, change-detection, anti-malware, physical access controls, logical access controls, audit logging, and segmentation controls.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','10.7.3','Requirement 10: Log and Monitor All Access to System Components and Cardholder Data','Security control failures are responded to','Failures of any critical security control systems are responded to promptly, including restoring functions, identifying and documenting the duration and cause, identifying and addressing any security issues, and resuming monitoring.','corrective','high'),

  -- Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly
  ('pci-dss','11.1.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Security policies and procedures for Requirement 11 are documented','All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 11 are documented, kept up to date, in use, and known to all affected parties.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.1.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Roles and responsibilities for Requirement 11 are assigned','Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 11 are documented, assigned, and understood.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.2.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Wireless access points are managed','Authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are managed: the presence of wireless access points is tested for, all authorized and unauthorized access points are detected and identified, and testing/detection is performed at least once every three months.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.2.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Inventory of wireless access points is maintained','An inventory of authorized wireless access points is maintained, including a documented business justification.','preventive','low'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Internal vulnerability scans are performed','Internal vulnerability scans are performed at least once every three months, high-risk and critical vulnerabilities are resolved, rescans are performed to confirm resolution, and the scan tool is kept up to date.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.1.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Other vulnerabilities are managed','All other applicable vulnerabilities (those not ranked as high-risk or critical) found in internal scans are managed by addressing them based on the risk defined in the entity''s targeted risk analysis and performing rescans as needed.','corrective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.1.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Internal scans use authenticated scanning','Internal vulnerability scans are performed via authenticated scanning, with sufficient privileges for accounts used, where systems accept credentials for scanning.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.1.3','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Internal scans after significant change','Internal vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change, high-risk and critical vulnerabilities are resolved, and rescans are conducted as needed.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','External vulnerability scans are performed','External vulnerability scans are performed at least once every three months by a PCI SSC Approved Scanning Vendor (ASV), vulnerabilities are resolved to meet the ASV Program Guide passing criteria, and rescans are performed as needed.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.3.2.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','External scans after significant change','External vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change, vulnerabilities scored 4.0 or higher by the CVSS are resolved, and rescans are conducted as needed (scans conducted by a qualified party).','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Penetration testing methodology is defined','A penetration testing methodology is defined, documented, and implemented, covering industry-accepted approaches, coverage of the CDE perimeter and critical systems, testing from inside and outside the network, and retention of results.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Internal penetration testing is performed','Internal penetration testing is performed per the defined methodology at least once every 12 months and after any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change, by a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party with organizational independence.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.3','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','External penetration testing is performed','External penetration testing is performed per the defined methodology at least once every 12 months and after any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change, by a qualified resource with organizational independence.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.4','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Penetration test findings are corrected','Exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration testing are corrected in accordance with the entity''s assessment of the risk, and penetration testing is repeated to verify the corrections.','corrective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.5','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Segmentation controls are penetration tested','If segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration testing is performed on segmentation controls at least once every 12 months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods, to confirm they are operational and effective.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.6','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Service provider segmentation testing every six months','Additional requirement for service providers only: if segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration testing is performed on segmentation controls at least once every six months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.4.7','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Multi-tenant providers support customer penetration testing','Additional requirement for multi-tenant service providers only: multi-tenant service providers support their customers for external penetration testing, either by providing access or evidence that customer testing would not affect the security of other customers.','administrative','low'),
  ('pci-dss','11.5.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Intrusion detection and prevention is used','Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion-prevention techniques are used to detect and/or prevent intrusions into the network, all traffic is monitored at the perimeter and critical points of the CDE, personnel are alerted to suspected compromises, and all engines/baselines/signatures are kept up to date.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.5.1.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Covert malware communication channels are addressed','Additional requirement for service providers only: intrusion-detection and/or intrusion-prevention techniques detect, alert on/prevent, and address covert malware communication channels.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','11.5.2','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Change-detection mechanism is deployed','A change-detection mechanism (for example, file integrity monitoring tools) is deployed to alert personnel to unauthorized modification of critical files, and to perform critical file comparisons at least once weekly.','detective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','11.6.1','Requirement 11: Test Security of Systems and Networks Regularly','Payment page change detection','A change- and tamper-detection mechanism is deployed for payment pages to alert personnel to unauthorized modification (including indicators of compromise) to the HTTP headers and contents of payment pages as received by the consumer browser, evaluated at least once every seven days.','detective','high'),

  -- Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs
  ('pci-dss','12.1.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Information security policy is established','An overall information security policy is established, published, maintained, and disseminated to all relevant personnel, as well as to relevant vendors and business partners.','governance','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.1.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Information security policy is reviewed','The information security policy is reviewed at least once every 12 months and updated as needed to reflect changes to business objectives or risks to the environment.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.1.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Security roles and responsibilities are defined','The security policy clearly defines information security roles and responsibilities for all personnel, and all personnel are aware of and acknowledge their information security responsibilities.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.1.4','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Responsibility for information security is assigned to executive','Responsibility for information security is formally assigned to a Chief Information Security Officer or other information security knowledgeable member of executive management.','governance','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.2.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Acceptable use policies are implemented','Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are documented and implemented, including explicit approval by authorized parties, acceptable uses, and a list of products approved for use.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.3.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Targeted risk analyses support flexible requirements','Each PCI DSS requirement that provides flexibility for how frequently it is performed is supported by a targeted risk analysis that is documented, reviewed at least once every 12 months, and defines the frequency for the activity.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.3.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Targeted risk analysis for customized approach','A targeted risk analysis is performed for each PCI DSS requirement that the entity meets with the customized approach, documenting the controls in place and providing evidence they meet the customized approach objective.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.3.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Cryptographic cipher suites are reviewed','Cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use are documented and reviewed at least once every 12 months, including an up-to-date inventory and a plan to respond to anticipated changes in cryptographic vulnerabilities.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.3.4','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Hardware and software technologies are reviewed','Hardware and software technologies in use are reviewed at least once every 12 months, including monitoring for technologies no longer supported by the vendor and developing a plan to remediate outdated technologies.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.4.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Executive responsibility for compliance program','Additional requirement for service providers only: responsibility is established by executive management for the protection of cardholder data and a PCI DSS compliance program, including overall accountability and a charter and communication to executive management.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.4.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Compliance reviews are performed quarterly','Additional requirement for service providers only: reviews are performed at least once every three months to confirm that personnel are performing their tasks in accordance with all security policies and operational procedures.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.4.2.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Compliance reviews are documented','Additional requirement for service providers only: reviews conducted per Requirement 12.4.2 are documented, including results, and reviewed and signed off by personnel assigned responsibility for the PCI DSS compliance program.','detective','low'),
  ('pci-dss','12.5.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Inventory of in-scope system components','An inventory of system components that are in scope for PCI DSS, including a description of function/use, is maintained and kept current.','preventive','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.5.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed','PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every 12 months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment.','governance','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.5.2.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Service provider scope confirmed every six months','Additional requirement for service providers only: PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every six months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.5.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Organizational change triggers scope review','Additional requirement for service providers only: significant changes to organizational structure result in a documented (internal) review of the impact to PCI DSS scope and applicability of controls, with results communicated to executive management.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.6.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Security awareness program is implemented','A formal security awareness program is implemented to make all personnel aware of the entity''s information security policy and procedures, and their role in protecting the cardholder data.','administrative','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.6.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Security awareness program is reviewed','The security awareness program is reviewed at least once every 12 months and updated as needed to address any new threats and vulnerabilities that may impact the security of the CDE, or the information provided to personnel about their role in protecting cardholder data.','administrative','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.6.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Personnel receive security awareness training','Personnel receive security awareness training upon hire and at least once every 12 months, acknowledge at least once every 12 months that they have read and understood the information security policy and procedures, and training covers multiple methods of communication.','administrative','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.6.3.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Training covers threats and social engineering','Security awareness training includes awareness of threats and vulnerabilities that could impact the security of the CDE, including but not limited to phishing and related attacks and social engineering.','administrative','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.6.3.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Training covers acceptable use','Security awareness training includes awareness about the acceptable use of end-user technologies in accordance with Requirement 12.2.1.','administrative','low'),
  ('pci-dss','12.7.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Personnel are screened','Potential personnel who will have access to the CDE are screened, within the constraints of local laws, prior to hire to minimize the risk of attacks from internal sources.','administrative','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.8.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','List of third-party service providers is maintained','A list of all third-party service providers (TPSPs) with which account data is shared or that could affect the security of account data is maintained, including a description of the services provided.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.8.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained','Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained, and include acknowledgements from TPSPs that they are responsible for the security of account data they possess or otherwise store, process, or transmit on behalf of the entity, or that could affect the security of the entity''s CDE.','governance','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.8.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Process for engaging TPSPs is implemented','An established process is implemented for engaging TPSPs, including proper due diligence prior to engagement.','preventive','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.8.4','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','TPSP compliance status is monitored','A program is implemented to monitor TPSPs'' PCI DSS compliance status at least once every 12 months.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.8.5','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Responsibility matrix for TPSP requirements','Information is maintained about which PCI DSS requirements are managed by each TPSP, which are managed by the entity, and any that are shared between the TPSP and the entity.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.9.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','TPSPs acknowledge responsibility to customers','Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs acknowledge in writing to customers that they are responsible for the security of account data the TPSP possesses or otherwise stores, processes, or transmits on behalf of the customer, or to the extent they could impact the security of the customer''s CDE.','governance','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.9.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','TPSPs support customer information requests','Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs support their customers'' requests for information to meet Requirements 12.8.4 and 12.8.5 by providing PCI DSS compliance status information and information about which requirements are the responsibility of the TPSP versus the customer.','administrative','low'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Incident response plan exists','An incident response plan exists and is ready to be activated in the event of a suspected or confirmed security incident, covering roles, responsibilities, communication and contact strategies, incident response procedures, business recovery, data backup, legal requirements, and reference to the payment brands'' and acquirer''s requirements.','corrective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.2','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Incident response plan is reviewed and tested','At least once every 12 months, the security incident response plan is reviewed and the content is updated as needed, and the plan is tested, including all elements listed in Requirement 12.10.1.','detective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.3','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','24/7 incident response personnel are designated','Specific personnel are designated to be available on a 24/7 basis to respond to suspected or confirmed security incidents.','corrective','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.4','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Incident response personnel are trained','Personnel responsible for responding to suspected and confirmed security incidents are appropriately and periodically trained on their incident response responsibilities.','administrative','medium'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.4.1','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Frequency of incident response training is risk-based','The frequency of periodic training for incident response personnel is defined in the entity''s targeted risk analysis.','administrative','low'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.5','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Incident response monitors security alerts','The security incident response plan includes monitoring and responding to alerts from security monitoring systems, including but not limited to intrusion-detection/prevention systems, network security controls, change-detection mechanisms for critical files, the change- and tamper-detection mechanism on payment pages, and detection of unauthorized wireless access points.','corrective','high'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.6','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Incident response plan evolves with lessons learned','The security incident response plan is modified and evolved according to lessons learned and to incorporate industry developments.','corrective','low'),
  ('pci-dss','12.10.7','Requirement 12: Support Information Security with Organizational Policies and Programs','Response to unexpected stored PAN','Incident response procedures are in place, to be initiated upon the detection of stored PAN anywhere it is not expected, and include determining what to do if PAN is discovered outside the CDE, securing the data, and determining how the data ended up there.','corrective','medium')
) AS v(framework_id, control_ref, domain, title, description, control_type, priority)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET
  control_ref = EXCLUDED.control_ref, domain = EXCLUDED.domain,
  title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description,
  control_type = EXCLUDED.control_type, priority = EXCLUDED.priority;

-- ==========================================================================
-- 3. HIPAA catalog (Security Rule safeguards + Privacy & Breach Notification).
--    (R) = Required implementation specification; (A) = Addressable.
-- ==========================================================================
INSERT INTO public.framework_controls
  (id, org_id, framework_id, control_ref, domain, title, description, control_type, priority)
SELECT
  'fc-' || v.framework_id || '-' ||
    regexp_replace(regexp_replace(lower(v.control_ref), '[^a-z0-9]+', '-', 'g'), '(^-|-$)', '', 'g'),
  '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
  v.framework_id, v.control_ref, v.domain, v.title, v.description, v.control_type, v.priority
FROM (VALUES
  -- Administrative Safeguards (§164.308)
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(1)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Security Management Process','Standard: implement policies and procedures to prevent, detect, contain, and correct security violations.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(1)(ii)(A)','Administrative Safeguards','Risk Analysis (R)','Required: conduct an accurate and thorough assessment of the potential risks and vulnerabilities to the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of electronic protected health information held by the covered entity or business associate.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(1)(ii)(B)','Administrative Safeguards','Risk Management (R)','Required: implement security measures sufficient to reduce risks and vulnerabilities to a reasonable and appropriate level to comply with the general security standards.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(1)(ii)(C)','Administrative Safeguards','Sanction Policy (R)','Required: apply appropriate sanctions against workforce members who fail to comply with the security policies and procedures of the covered entity or business associate.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(1)(ii)(D)','Administrative Safeguards','Information System Activity Review (R)','Required: implement procedures to regularly review records of information system activity, such as audit logs, access reports, and security incident tracking reports.','detective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(2)','Administrative Safeguards','Assigned Security Responsibility','Standard (Required): identify the security official who is responsible for the development and implementation of the policies and procedures required by the Security Rule.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(3)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Workforce Security','Standard: implement policies and procedures to ensure that all members of the workforce have appropriate access to electronic protected health information, and to prevent those who do not have access from obtaining access.','administrative','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(3)(ii)(A)','Administrative Safeguards','Authorization and/or Supervision (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for the authorization and/or supervision of workforce members who work with electronic protected health information or in locations where it might be accessed.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(3)(ii)(B)','Administrative Safeguards','Workforce Clearance Procedure (A)','Addressable: implement procedures to determine that the access of a workforce member to electronic protected health information is appropriate.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(3)(ii)(C)','Administrative Safeguards','Termination Procedures (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for terminating access to electronic protected health information when the employment of, or other arrangement with, a workforce member ends.','preventive','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(4)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Information Access Management','Standard: implement policies and procedures for authorizing access to electronic protected health information consistent with the applicable requirements of the Privacy Rule.','administrative','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(4)(ii)(A)','Administrative Safeguards','Isolating Health Care Clearinghouse Functions (R)','Required: if a health care clearinghouse is part of a larger organization, implement policies and procedures that protect the electronic protected health information of the clearinghouse from unauthorized access by the larger organization.','preventive','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(4)(ii)(B)','Administrative Safeguards','Access Authorization (A)','Addressable: implement policies and procedures for granting access to electronic protected health information, for example, through access to a workstation, transaction, program, process, or other mechanism.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(4)(ii)(C)','Administrative Safeguards','Access Establishment and Modification (A)','Addressable: implement policies and procedures that, based upon the entity''s access authorization policies, establish, document, review, and modify a user''s right of access to a workstation, transaction, program, or process.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(5)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Security Awareness and Training','Standard: implement a security awareness and training program for all members of the workforce, including management.','administrative','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(5)(ii)(A)','Administrative Safeguards','Security Reminders (A)','Addressable: provide periodic security updates as part of the security awareness and training program.','administrative','low'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(5)(ii)(B)','Administrative Safeguards','Protection from Malicious Software (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for guarding against, detecting, and reporting malicious software.','preventive','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(5)(ii)(C)','Administrative Safeguards','Log-in Monitoring (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for monitoring log-in attempts and reporting discrepancies.','detective','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(5)(ii)(D)','Administrative Safeguards','Password Management (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for creating, changing, and safeguarding passwords.','preventive','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(6)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Security Incident Procedures','Standard: implement policies and procedures to address security incidents.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(6)(ii)','Administrative Safeguards','Response and Reporting (R)','Required: identify and respond to suspected or known security incidents; mitigate, to the extent practicable, harmful effects of security incidents that are known to the covered entity or business associate; and document security incidents and their outcomes.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(i)','Administrative Safeguards','Contingency Plan','Standard: establish (and implement as needed) policies and procedures for responding to an emergency or other occurrence (for example, fire, vandalism, system failure, and natural disaster) that damages systems that contain electronic protected health information.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(ii)(A)','Administrative Safeguards','Data Backup Plan (R)','Required: establish and implement procedures to create and maintain retrievable exact copies of electronic protected health information.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(ii)(B)','Administrative Safeguards','Disaster Recovery Plan (R)','Required: establish (and implement as needed) procedures to restore any loss of data.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(ii)(C)','Administrative Safeguards','Emergency Mode Operation Plan (R)','Required: establish (and implement as needed) procedures to enable continuation of critical business processes for protection of the security of electronic protected health information while operating in emergency mode.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(ii)(D)','Administrative Safeguards','Testing and Revision Procedures (A)','Addressable: implement procedures for periodic testing and revision of contingency plans.','detective','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(7)(ii)(E)','Administrative Safeguards','Applications and Data Criticality Analysis (A)','Addressable: assess the relative criticality of specific applications and data in support of other contingency plan components.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(a)(8)','Administrative Safeguards','Evaluation','Standard (Required): perform a periodic technical and nontechnical evaluation, based initially upon the standards implemented under the Security Rule and subsequently in response to environmental or operational changes affecting the security of electronic protected health information, that establishes the extent to which policies and procedures meet the requirements.','detective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(b)(1)','Administrative Safeguards','Business Associate Contracts and Other Arrangements','Standard: a covered entity may permit a business associate to create, receive, maintain, or transmit electronic protected health information on the covered entity''s behalf only if the covered entity obtains satisfactory assurances that the business associate will appropriately safeguard the information.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.308(b)(4)','Administrative Safeguards','Written Contract or Other Arrangement (R)','Required: document the satisfactory assurances required by the business associate contracts standard through a written contract or other arrangement with the business associate that meets the applicable requirements of §164.314(a).','governance','high'),

  -- Physical Safeguards (§164.310)
  ('hipaa','164.310(a)(1)','Physical Safeguards','Facility Access Controls','Standard: implement policies and procedures to limit physical access to electronic information systems and the facility or facilities in which they are housed, while ensuring that properly authorized access is allowed.','physical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(a)(2)(i)','Physical Safeguards','Contingency Operations (A)','Addressable: establish (and implement as needed) procedures that allow facility access in support of restoration of lost data under the disaster recovery plan and emergency mode operations plan in the event of an emergency.','physical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(a)(2)(ii)','Physical Safeguards','Facility Security Plan (A)','Addressable: implement policies and procedures to safeguard the facility and the equipment therein from unauthorized physical access, tampering, and theft.','physical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(a)(2)(iii)','Physical Safeguards','Access Control and Validation Procedures (A)','Addressable: implement procedures to control and validate a person''s access to facilities based on their role or function, including visitor control, and control of access to software programs for testing and revision.','physical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(a)(2)(iv)','Physical Safeguards','Maintenance Records (A)','Addressable: implement policies and procedures to document repairs and modifications to the physical components of a facility which are related to security (for example, hardware, walls, doors, and locks).','physical','low'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(b)','Physical Safeguards','Workstation Use','Standard (Required): implement policies and procedures that specify the proper functions to be performed, the manner in which those functions are to be performed, and the physical attributes of the surroundings of a specific workstation or class of workstation that can access electronic protected health information.','physical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(c)','Physical Safeguards','Workstation Security','Standard (Required): implement physical safeguards for all workstations that access electronic protected health information, to restrict access to authorized users.','physical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(d)(1)','Physical Safeguards','Device and Media Controls','Standard: implement policies and procedures that govern the receipt and removal of hardware and electronic media that contain electronic protected health information into and out of a facility, and the movement of these items within the facility.','physical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(d)(2)(i)','Physical Safeguards','Disposal (R)','Required: implement policies and procedures to address the final disposition of electronic protected health information, and/or the hardware or electronic media on which it is stored.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(d)(2)(ii)','Physical Safeguards','Media Re-use (R)','Required: implement procedures for removal of electronic protected health information from electronic media before the media are made available for re-use.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(d)(2)(iii)','Physical Safeguards','Accountability (A)','Addressable: maintain a record of the movements of hardware and electronic media and any person responsible therefore.','detective','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.310(d)(2)(iv)','Physical Safeguards','Data Backup and Storage (A)','Addressable: create a retrievable, exact copy of electronic protected health information, when needed, before movement of equipment.','corrective','medium'),

  -- Technical Safeguards (§164.312)
  ('hipaa','164.312(a)(1)','Technical Safeguards','Access Control','Standard: implement technical policies and procedures for electronic information systems that maintain electronic protected health information to allow access only to those persons or software programs that have been granted access rights as specified in §164.308(a)(4).','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(a)(2)(i)','Technical Safeguards','Unique User Identification (R)','Required: assign a unique name and/or number for identifying and tracking user identity.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(a)(2)(ii)','Technical Safeguards','Emergency Access Procedure (R)','Required: establish (and implement as needed) procedures for obtaining necessary electronic protected health information during an emergency.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(a)(2)(iii)','Technical Safeguards','Automatic Logoff (A)','Addressable: implement electronic procedures that terminate an electronic session after a predetermined time of inactivity.','technical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(a)(2)(iv)','Technical Safeguards','Encryption and Decryption (A)','Addressable: implement a mechanism to encrypt and decrypt electronic protected health information.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(b)','Technical Safeguards','Audit Controls','Standard (Required): implement hardware, software, and/or procedural mechanisms that record and examine activity in information systems that contain or use electronic protected health information.','detective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(c)(1)','Technical Safeguards','Integrity','Standard: implement policies and procedures to protect electronic protected health information from improper alteration or destruction.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(c)(2)','Technical Safeguards','Mechanism to Authenticate ePHI (A)','Addressable: implement electronic mechanisms to corroborate that electronic protected health information has not been altered or destroyed in an unauthorized manner.','technical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(d)','Technical Safeguards','Person or Entity Authentication','Standard (Required): implement procedures to verify that a person or entity seeking access to electronic protected health information is the one claimed.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(e)(1)','Technical Safeguards','Transmission Security','Standard: implement technical security measures to guard against unauthorized access to electronic protected health information that is being transmitted over an electronic communications network.','technical','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(e)(2)(i)','Technical Safeguards','Integrity Controls (A)','Addressable: implement security measures to ensure that electronically transmitted electronic protected health information is not improperly modified without detection until disposed of.','technical','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.312(e)(2)(ii)','Technical Safeguards','Encryption (A)','Addressable: implement a mechanism to encrypt electronic protected health information whenever deemed appropriate.','technical','high'),

  -- Organizational Requirements (§164.314)
  ('hipaa','164.314(a)(1)','Organizational Requirements','Business Associate Contracts or Other Arrangements','Standard: the contract or other arrangement between the covered entity and its business associate required by §164.308(b) must meet the requirements of this section, as applicable.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.314(a)(2)(i)','Organizational Requirements','Business Associate Contracts (R)','Required: the contract must provide that the business associate will comply with the applicable requirements of the Security Rule, ensure any subcontractors that create, receive, maintain, or transmit ePHI agree to comply, and report security incidents to the covered entity.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.314(a)(2)(ii)','Organizational Requirements','Other Arrangements (R)','Required: address the manner in which the requirements are satisfied when a covered entity and its business associate are both governmental entities, or where other law provides authorization.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.314(a)(2)(iii)','Organizational Requirements','Business Associate Contracts with Subcontractors (R)','Required: the requirements applicable to contracts between a covered entity and business associate apply in the same manner to contracts between a business associate and a subcontractor.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.314(b)(1)','Organizational Requirements','Requirements for Group Health Plans','Standard: except when the only ePHI disclosed to a plan sponsor is disclosed pursuant to §164.504(f)(1)(ii) or (iii), a group health plan must ensure that its plan documents provide that the plan sponsor will reasonably and appropriately safeguard ePHI.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.314(b)(2)','Organizational Requirements','Group Health Plan Implementation Specifications (R)','Required: the plan documents of the group health plan must require the plan sponsor to implement administrative, physical, and technical safeguards; ensure adequate separation; ensure agents safeguard ePHI; and report security incidents.','governance','medium'),

  -- Policies and Procedures and Documentation Requirements (§164.316)
  ('hipaa','164.316(a)','Policies and Documentation','Policies and Procedures','Standard: implement reasonable and appropriate policies and procedures to comply with the standards, implementation specifications, or other requirements of the Security Rule.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.316(b)(1)','Policies and Documentation','Documentation','Standard: maintain the policies and procedures implemented to comply with the Security Rule in written (which may be electronic) form, and if an action, activity, or assessment is required to be documented, maintain a written record of it.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.316(b)(2)(i)','Policies and Documentation','Time Limit (R)','Required: retain the documentation required by the Security Rule for six years from the date of its creation or the date when it last was in effect, whichever is later.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.316(b)(2)(ii)','Policies and Documentation','Availability (R)','Required: make documentation available to those persons responsible for implementing the procedures to which the documentation pertains.','administrative','low'),
  ('hipaa','164.316(b)(2)(iii)','Policies and Documentation','Updates (R)','Required: review documentation periodically, and update as needed, in response to environmental or operational changes affecting the security of the electronic protected health information.','governance','medium'),

  -- Privacy Rule (Subpart E) — key provisions
  ('hipaa','164.502','Privacy Rule','Uses and disclosures of protected health information: General rules','A covered entity or business associate may not use or disclose protected health information except as permitted or required by the Privacy Rule, including the minimum necessary standard and business associate provisions.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.506','Privacy Rule','Uses and disclosures to carry out treatment, payment, or health care operations','A covered entity may use or disclose protected health information for its own treatment, payment, and health care operations, and in certain circumstances for the treatment, payment, and operations of another covered entity, without an authorization.','governance','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.508','Privacy Rule','Uses and disclosures for which an authorization is required','Except as otherwise permitted or required, a covered entity may not use or disclose protected health information without a valid authorization, and when obtained the use or disclosure must be consistent with that authorization; specific authorization is required for psychotherapy notes and most marketing and sale of PHI.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.514','Privacy Rule','Other requirements relating to uses and disclosures of PHI','Sets out de-identification standards, the minimum necessary requirements, limited data sets and data use agreements, and other conditions on uses and disclosures of protected health information.','governance','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.524','Privacy Rule','Access of individuals to protected health information','An individual has a right of access to inspect and obtain a copy of protected health information about the individual in a designated record set, for as long as the information is maintained, subject to limited exceptions and required timeframes.','administrative','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.526','Privacy Rule','Amendment of protected health information','An individual has the right to have a covered entity amend protected health information or a record about the individual in a designated record set for as long as the information is maintained, subject to specified grounds for denial and procedures.','administrative','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.528','Privacy Rule','Accounting of disclosures of protected health information','An individual has a right to receive an accounting of disclosures of protected health information made by a covered entity in the six years prior to the request, subject to specified exceptions.','detective','medium'),

  -- Breach Notification Rule (Subpart D)
  ('hipaa','164.404','Breach Notification','Notification to individuals','A covered entity must, following the discovery of a breach of unsecured protected health information, notify each individual whose unsecured PHI has been, or is reasonably believed to have been, accessed, acquired, used, or disclosed as a result of the breach, without unreasonable delay and no later than 60 days after discovery.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.406','Breach Notification','Notification to the media','For a breach of unsecured protected health information involving more than 500 residents of a State or jurisdiction, a covered entity must notify prominent media outlets serving that State or jurisdiction, without unreasonable delay and no later than 60 days after discovery.','corrective','medium'),
  ('hipaa','164.408','Breach Notification','Notification to the Secretary','A covered entity must notify the Secretary of HHS of breaches of unsecured protected health information; breaches involving 500 or more individuals are reported contemporaneously with individual notice, and smaller breaches are logged and reported annually.','corrective','high'),
  ('hipaa','164.410','Breach Notification','Notification by a business associate','A business associate must, following the discovery of a breach of unsecured protected health information, notify the covered entity of the breach without unreasonable delay and no later than 60 days after discovery, and include the identification of each affected individual to the extent possible.','corrective','high')
) AS v(framework_id, control_ref, domain, title, description, control_type, priority)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET
  control_ref = EXCLUDED.control_ref, domain = EXCLUDED.domain,
  title = EXCLUDED.title, description = EXCLUDED.description,
  control_type = EXCLUDED.control_type, priority = EXCLUDED.priority;

-- ==========================================================================
-- 4. Sync control_count from the seeded catalog + emit proof.
-- ==========================================================================
UPDATE public.frameworks f
SET control_count = (SELECT count(*) FROM public.framework_controls fc
                     WHERE fc.framework_id = f.id
                       AND fc.org_id = '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001')
WHERE f.id IN ('pci-dss','hipaa');

DO $$
DECLARE
  n_pci   INTEGER;
  n_hipaa INTEGER;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_pci   FROM public.framework_controls
    WHERE framework_id = 'pci-dss' AND org_id = '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_hipaa FROM public.framework_controls
    WHERE framework_id = 'hipaa'   AND org_id = '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';
  RAISE NOTICE 'seed_catalog_pci_hipaa: pci-dss=% controls, hipaa=% controls', n_pci, n_hipaa;
END $$;
